# Customer-Churn-Prediction
Customer Churn Prediction  A Machine Learning web application that predicts whether a customer is likely to churn based on customer demographics, subscription details, payment method, monthly charges, and tenure.

The project uses Python, Pandas, Scikit-learn, Joblib, and Streamlit. 
A complete machine learning pipeline is used for preprocessing categorical and numerical features, training the classification model, and making predictions through an interactive Streamlit interface.

Features
Customer churn prediction using Machine Learning
Categorical feature preprocessing using OneHotEncoder
Numerical and categorical feature handling using ColumnTransformer
Complete preprocessing and model pipeline using Scikit-learn Pipeline
Interactive Streamlit web application
Customer input form for real-time predictions
Visual prediction results for churn and non-churn customers
Model saved and loaded using Joblib

Technologies Used:
Python
Pandas
NumPy
Scikit-learn
Joblib
Streamlit
Project Workflow

SQL Database → Data Processing → EDA → Preprocessing → Model Training → Pipeline → Model Saving → Streamlit Deployment

This project demonstrates an end-to-end Machine Learning workflow, from data preparation and model development to deployment as a web application.
